# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Contour — AI before/after configuration
# Copy to .env.local for local dev; set the same vars in Vercel
# (Project Settings -> Environment Variables) for deployment.
#
# With NO keys set, the app still runs fully: the visualization
# uses the on-device landmark-warp simulation and tells the user
# photoreal AI is not configured. Add a key for the real magic.
#
# Three providers are wired so you can run the KB's model bake-off:
# same rhinoplasty edit, same 3-4 faces, whichever holds identity
# best wins. Flip AI_PROVIDER to compare them like-for-like.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Provider 1 (recommended default): Google Gemini image editing
# (Nano Banana family). Best-in-class identity preservation, which is
# the whole game for "same face, new nose". Key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Default gemini-2.5-flash-image (Nano Banana). Set gemini-3-pro-image
# (Nano Banana Pro) when your key has access for higher fidelity.
GEMINI_IMAGE_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-image

# --- Provider 2: OpenAI GPT Image 2. Stronger at complex spatial
# reasoning (e.g. combined chin+nose profile balancing); we send
# input_fidelity=high to protect the patient's face. Key: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Default gpt-image-1. Set gpt-image-2 when available on your account.
OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1

# --- Provider 3: FLUX.1 Kontext (Black Forest Labs). Controllable
# instructed editing, good for self-hosting later. https://api.bfl.ai
BFL_API_KEY=
BFL_MODEL=flux-kontext-pro

# --- Provider 4: Higgsfield Cloud (platform.higgsfield.ai). Key ID +
# secret from cloud.higgsfield.ai; note the API bills from its own credit
# wallet, SEPARATE from any Higgsfield app subscription - top up under
# Billing on cloud.higgsfield.ai. Models on this router: reve/edit
# (instruction photo editing, default), higgsfield-ai/soul/reference,
# higgsfield-ai/soul/character (reference-guided renders). Nano Banana is
# NOT exposed through the Higgsfield API.
HIGGSFIELD_API_KEY=
HIGGSFIELD_API_SECRET=
HIGGSFIELD_IMAGE_MODEL=reve/edit

# Force one provider: "gemini" | "openai" | "flux" | "higgsfield".
# Leave blank to auto-detect (priority: gemini -> openai -> flux ->
# higgsfield, with the others as automatic fallbacks). Set it to run a
# controlled bake-off.
AI_PROVIDER=

# --- Assessment skin analysis (VISION model, not image editing) --------
# The Assessment Report's AI half reads the front photo and classifies it
# against a locked skin taxonomy (photo -> findings text). This is image
# UNDERSTANDING; it is a DIFFERENT job from the before/after image EDIT
# above. Priority: Claude -> OpenAI -> Gemini, each a fallback for the one
# before. With none set, the report still renders its proportion analysis.
#
# Claude is recommended here: strongest vision read, most reliable
# structured JSON, and it keeps the report on one vendor. Key:
# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# NOTE: no Anthropic model can GENERATE the before/after image — that needs
# an image model (Gemini / Higgsfield above). This key powers findings only.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Default claude-opus-4-8 (best). Set claude-haiku-4-5 or claude-sonnet-5
# to cut cost/latency if you run a high volume of scans.
ANTHROPIC_VISION_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
# OpenAI vision fallback model (used only when Claude is unset or errors and
# OPENAI_API_KEY is set). Default gpt-4o.
ASSESSMENT_VISION_MODEL=gpt-4o

# --- Booth link (phone -> desktop patient handoff) ---------------------
# Vercel: Storage -> Create -> Blob -> connect to this project. Vercel
# injects BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN automatically on deploy; for local dev
# against real Blob, paste the token here. With no token, local dev uses
# a file-based inbox (.booth-dev-store/) and production returns a clear
# "not configured" message. Inbox items auto-expire after 24 hours.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# --- Multi-tenancy: database (REQUIRED for real multi-clinic use) ------
# Neon/Vercel Postgres. Vercel injects POSTGRES_URL/DATABASE_URL when you
# connect a database (Storage -> Create -> Postgres). This is the system of
# record: clinics, staff, patients, appointments, calls, portal, usage — all
# clinic-scoped. Without it the app cannot isolate clinics or persist data.
DATABASE_URL=

# --- Auth session signing ----------------------------------------------
# Secret used to sign the session cookie (HS256). If unset, it is derived
# (SHA-256) from DATABASE_URL, so auth works out of the box — but set a
# dedicated 32+ char random value in production so rotating the DB URL does
# not invalidate every session.
SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Clinic provisioning (platform superuser) --------------------------
# Required in production to create new clinics via /api/admin/provision
# (and scripts/provision-clinic.mjs). Any strong random string; keep it
# secret. Without it, provisioning is allowed only in local dev.
PLATFORM_ADMIN_KEY=

# --- VYBERO voice agent -------------------------------------------------
# Shared platform key the voice agent sends as the x-vybero-key header on
# availability / book / call-log calls. The agent identifies its clinic with
# an x-clinic header (the clinic's slug or id), so one key serves all clinics
# while each agent writes ONLY to its own clinic. Clinic screens use the
# session cookie instead and never need this.
VYBERO_API_KEY=

# Optional: default clinic hours the agent honors if a clinic has not set
# its own in Settings, e.g. {"open":"10:00","close":"19:00","slot_min":30,"days":[1,2,3,4,5,6]}
CLINIC_HOURS=

# --- ElevenLabs call-history sync ---------------------------------------
# API key from elevenlabs.io (profile -> API keys). Powers
# /api/vybero/sync-elevenlabs: Vercel Cron pulls Noor's conversations into
# the Analytics call log daily (03:00 UTC = 08:00 PKT), and the VYBERO
# page's "Sync calls" button runs it on demand. Without it the sync
# answers 501 and analytics shows only what the post-call webhook pushes.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# Optional: set to protect the cron endpoint; Vercel sends it as a Bearer
# header on scheduled invocations automatically.
CRON_SECRET=

# --- Demo seed gate ------------------------------------------------------
# By default an EMPTY database seeds the CAPTURE demo clinic (staff,
# patients, invoices, reviews) on first login — perfect for demos.
# Set SEED_DEMO=false on a REAL production deployment so fake data can
# never mix with client data; provision clean clinics via
# /api/admin/provision instead.
SEED_DEMO=
